In May 2025, Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/05/15/apples-carplay-ultra-now-available/">launched CarPlay Ultra</a>, the long-awaited next-generation version of CarPlay that it first previewed in 2022. More than a year later, however, CarPlay Ultra is still <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/05/15/first-look-at-carplay-ultra/">limited to select Aston Martin vehicles</a> with six-figure price tags.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/Aston-Martin-CarPlay-Ultra-Screen.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1034779" /><br/>
In a <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2025/05/carplay-ultra-the-next-generation-of-carplay-begins-rolling-out-today/">press release</a> last year, Apple said "many" other vehicle brands around the world planned to offer CarPlay Ultra, including Hyundai, Kia, and Genesis. Yet, more than 15 months have passed since that announcement, and the software has still not expanded beyond Aston Martin. Apple has not provided any further updates on CarPlay Ultra availability.<br/>
<br/>
CarPlay Ultra features deeper integration with a vehicle's instrument cluster and systems, built-in apps for radio and climate controls, rear-view camera feed support, and more. The connected iPhone provides app-related data, while the vehicle provides information like the current speed, fuel level, tire pressure, engine temperature, and more.<br/>
<br/>
The interface is tailored to each vehicle model and automaker's identity, and drivers can choose from various preset design options.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/Aston-Martin-CarPlay-Ultra-Climate-Controls.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1034780" /><br/>
